  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Saturday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Satellite loop is showing nothing in the\nway of cloud cover across northern and central Nevada this\nafternoon. Expect a cool night with lows in the 30s and clear\nskies.\n\nDry and warm conditions continue to dominate in the short term as\na dry pattern remains over the forecast area. High temperatures \nMonday and Tuesday afternoons are expected to be in the 60s and \n70s. Overnight lows for Monday and Tuesday night will be in the \n30s and 40s.\n\nAll models are depicting an upper level low pressure system diving\nto the south from the Pacific Northwest states to just off the\ncoast of western California late Tuesday. Light valley rain \nshowers and mountain snow showers are expected to develop during \nthe latter portions of the afternoon and overnight period. Winds \nwill be breezy to locally windy with gusts of 25 to 40 mph. Highs \nwill be several degrees cooler with readings in the 50s and 60s. \nOvernight lows will be in the 30s and 40s.\n\nA slow forward progression is in store for this storm system as it\ntries to move east across northern and central Nevada Wednesday\nand Thursday. Valley rain showers and mountain snow showers are\nagain possible both days. The estimated three day forecast amounts\nfor precipitation and snowfall are coming in around one-half to \ntwo-thirds of an inch of rainfall in the valleys with one to four\ninches across the highest elevations in the mountains. Afternoon\nhighs both of these days will be in the 50s and 60s with overnight\nlows in the 30s and 40s.\n\nThe system may be exiting east by the latter portions of the \nweek. Highs will remain on the cool side with readings in the 50s \nand 60s and lows in the 30s.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: No changes were made to the\nshort term grids as NBM is handling the forecast well. Confidence\nin the forecast remains high through Monday. Confidence continues\nto be moderate with respect to the precipitation and temperature \nforecast next week. Low confidence on the chances of a cold front\nlate next week.",
